      "problem": "Evaluate the indicator function\n$1[7\\in \\{2,4,6,10\\}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the predicate is $7\\in \\{2,4,6,10\\}.$ Since $7$ is not an element of the set $\\{2,4,6,10\\},$ the predicate is false. Therefore,\n\n$$\n1[7\\in \\{2,4,6,10\\}]=0.\n$$",
